      "id": "NBT-01",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-branching-test-translate",
      "title": "Finding a smooth test that detects a given occurrence",
      "hypotheses": "G=U(p,q) and H=U(p−1,q) satisfy the separated branching hypotheses. A discrete series σ occurs in π|H through a nonzero bounded H-map. Fix Haar measure, its reciprocal formal degree κ>0, and a unit vector w in the lowest compact type of σ.",
      "statement": "There exists a smooth unit ambient vector η, obtained by translating an ambient lowest-type vector, for which the smaller-group coefficient average Rη is nonzero.",
      "definitions": [
        "The coefficient φ(h) is the complex conjugate of ⟨w,σ(h)w⟩. The gap bound gives its absolute integrability.",
        "The linear functional L(a)=⟨jw,Ra⟩ is continuous in the ambient Hilbert norm."
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "equations": [
        "normalization-branching-test-detector"
      ],
