    {
      "id": "NBT-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-branching-test-normalization",
      "title": "Normalizing the occurrence for a single test vector",
      "hypotheses": "Fix w, κ, π, σ and a smooth η as in the test-translate result, with Rη nonzero. The Haar measure is invariant under inversion.",
      "statement": "There exists an isometric H-intertwiner i such that ⟨η,iw⟩ is a positive real number and ⟨η,Ra⟩=κ⟨η,iw⟩⟨iw,a⟩ for every ambient a. The copy i and the first test vector are selected together, allowing further copies of σ.",
      "definitions": [
        "R is integration against φ in the ambient restriction. R*=R and R²=κR.",
        "For r=‖Rη‖ the unnormalized intertwiner J has Jw=Rη, and J*J=r²Id. Its normalization is i=J/r."
      ],
